  "title": "Why 2025 Is a Gold Rush Year for Business Buyers",
  "date": "2025-08-19T14:31:21.377Z",
  "content": {
    "text": "96\n\n Why 2025 Is a Gold Rush Year for Business Buyers\nHi Sara,\nThere\u2019s a perfect storm brewing in the business world\u2014and for once, it\u2019s good news.\n2025 has been the biggest year ever for small business acquisitions, and no, that\u2019s not just LinkedIn hype. I\u2019m on the front lines as a deal attorney to small deals, and what I\u2019m seeing is a tidal wave of buyers and sellers finally meeting in the middle.\u00a0\nHere's why:\n1. Boomers Are Out (and There Are a Lot of Them)\nCall it the \u201csilver tsunami\u201d if you must, but Baby Boomers are done. Sellers in their 70s, 80s, even 90s are still hanging on, hoping to sell to the next generation\u2026 who mostly say, \u201cThanks, but no thanks.\u201d That leaves a huge inventory of businesses with no succession plan. Opportunity is knocking.\n2. Millennials and Gen X Want Freedom\nForget the corner office. This generation wants autonomy, flexibility, and control\u2014not another round of soul-sucking meetings. Self-employment isn\u2019t a fringe idea anymore\u2014it\u2019s a career goal.\n3. The Startup Dream? Kinda Dead\nRemember the \u201cUber for X\u201d phase? Yeah, so do I. I represented a lot of those companies, and let me tell you\u2014those glossy press releases rarely matched the reality (behind the scenes those billion dollar exits were rarely as exciting as they sound). Entrepreneurs are now wiser, more risk-averse, and looking for cash flow, not chaos.\n4. Search Funds Are Booming\nEntrepreneurship-through-acquisition is the new startup. You get to run a business, make it better, and skip the painful zero-to-one stage. It\u2019s a safer bet for ambitious people who want ROI and can afford their life at the same time.\n5. Real Estate\u2019s Tough, Crypto\u2019s Weird, Stocks Are Stressful\nHigh interest rates have made real estate as an investment play less attractive. Crypto lost its edge now that it tracks the stock market. The stock market? Yawn. People want something tangible, profitable, and slightly less roller-coastery. Enter: small business acquisition.\n6. Post-Pandemic Priorities Have Shifted\nWorking from home changed everything. People tasted freedom and liked it. Then came the return-to-office mandates, layoffs, and existential crises. Now, many are asking, \u201cWhy not just buy a business?\u201d And they\u2019re right to ask.\nBottom line?\n\nWe\u2019ve got more sellers than ever. More buyers than ever. And more deals are happening than ever. It\u2019s raining transactions in 2025.\nIf you\u2019re thinking about buying (or selling) a business, now is not the time to sit on the sidelines. Head to Deal Academy to get expert insights, tools, and actual legal intel\u2014not recycled Twitter threads, I swear.\nTo smarter deals and bold moves,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nFounder, Deal Academy\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
